                      <Parameter id="lk7Ej87GdkWQQh1LJarm8g" name="Gastric emptying time" description="The time at which the (1-1/e)th part (approximately 63%) of the applied dose (fasted state) is released from the stomach into the duodenum according to a first order process. Please note that in the case that a meal is co-administered with the drug, the gastric emptying rate is described using a Weibull function. The parameters of the Weibull function and, thus, the gastric emptying time, then depend on the volume and composition of the meal" icon="Parameter" persistable="0" isFixedValue="0" dim="Time" quantityType="Parameter" negativeValuesAllowed="1" value="15" displayUnit="min">
